                <pb facs="0154" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.572/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schmedeman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-04T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 4,
                                1919, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>672. At request of Norwegian Government, denunciation of Treaty of Commerce and
                    Navigation of July 4, 1827, contained in the note of the American Minister at
                    Christiania of February 2, 1918 to the Norwegian Foreign Office was formally
                    withdrawn on February 1 except as to articles 13 and 14 of the Treaty.
                    Consequently the Treaty of Commerce and Navigation of July 4, 1827, except
                    articles 13 and 14, which expired on February 2, 1919, remains as to Norway in
                    full force and effect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
